01:18:24.725 --> 01:18:28.565
which is unfortunate because that's a really tight timetable

01:18:28.885 --> 01:18:31.765
to do what it is that they've asked.

01:18:32.325 --> 01:18:36.805
So the good news is they approved 30 and bonded $30,000,000

01:18:36.805 --> 01:18:37.445
in funding.

01:18:38.120 --> 01:18:39.560
There's 130

01:18:39.560 --> 01:18:44.919
towns that are eligible for steep grant funding because big cities are not.

01:18:46.200 --> 01:18:47.960
There's a $500,000

01:18:47.960 --> 01:18:49.480
max grant amount.

01:18:50.520 --> 01:18:54.765
So if every single town applied for the maximum amount,

01:18:55.165 --> 01:18:58.205
there's a fiftyfifty chance we would get the grant.

01:18:59.485 --> 01:19:03.805
But the reality is when you look through past years, not everybody submits.

01:19:04.320 --> 01:19:07.760
So I would anticipate probably a 100 towns

01:19:08.160 --> 01:19:09.840
submitting a steep grant,

01:19:10.400 --> 01:19:12.880
maybe even a little less because of the tight

01:19:13.120 --> 01:19:17.760
time window. And not everybody will go for the max grant award,

01:19:18.925 --> 01:19:22.845
which is another way of saying that if you put out a good grant,

01:19:23.085 --> 01:19:24.205
there's

01:19:24.205 --> 01:19:26.285
a better than 75%

01:19:26.285 --> 01:19:27.085
chance

01:19:27.165 --> 01:19:28.445
that we'll get it,

01:19:29.085 --> 01:19:40.340
which is why I'm willing to expend a lot of energy to put this thing out there because I think we have a reasonable chance of getting it. Our track record of getting steep grants is pretty good.

01:19:42.260 --> 01:19:45.300
There's two issues with this grant submission.

01:19:45.940 --> 01:19:47.860
The first thing is

01:19:48.075 --> 01:19:51.435
they put a really high, they don't mandate

01:19:51.995 --> 01:19:53.515
that the town

01:19:53.835 --> 01:19:56.395
has matching funds for it.

01:19:56.875 --> 01:19:59.195
But they also said very clearly

01:19:59.275 --> 01:20:01.115
that they will not evaluate

01:20:01.115 --> 01:20:03.610
any grant that doesn't have 20%

01:20:03.610 --> 01:20:04.970
matching funds

01:20:05.370 --> 01:20:07.290
unless they can't fill

01:20:08.970 --> 01:20:12.089
the pool with grants that do.

01:20:13.370 --> 01:20:18.475
So in other words, basically the first cut they're making at these grant applications

01:20:18.715 --> 01:20:23.675
is who can guarantee they've got 20% matching funds.

01:20:24.155 --> 01:20:25.435
Now, in this case,

01:20:25.835 --> 01:20:28.395
because we have a multi use

01:20:28.130 --> 01:20:28.770
or

01:20:29.250 --> 01:20:30.690
building fund

01:20:30.850 --> 01:20:33.730
that we can tap for matching funds,

01:20:34.610 --> 01:20:37.250
we have an easy way to meet the 20%

01:20:37.250 --> 01:20:38.210
requirement.

01:20:38.450 --> 01:20:42.245
So, that's one of the reasons why the Board of Selectmen agreed with this

01:20:42.725 --> 01:20:45.365
being our steep grant project.

01:20:45.925 --> 01:20:52.005
And the second thing the state has made a really high priority on, and that's because in the past,

01:20:53.010 --> 01:20:54.930
you know, towns

01:20:55.010 --> 01:21:00.209
often took four or five years to actually execute their steep grant projects.

01:21:00.530 --> 01:21:08.125
So, and they kind of changed them or they changed the scope or they did all these things. So, the state has said no more of that crap.

01:21:09.565 --> 01:21:19.325
We are going to only fund projects that are shovel ready or near shovel ready. And we can talk about that a little bit before.

01:21:19.805 --> 01:21:20.045
